        "# Agent Observability: Langfuse, Phoenix, Opik Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements a stdlib trace collector + LLM-judge evaluator:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Ingest GenAI-shaped spans."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Group by session, tag failed runs (guardrail trips, low-confidence evals)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A scripted LLM-judge that scores agent responses on a rubric."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A dashboard-like summary: failure rate, top failure reasons, eval score distribution."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Output: per-session eval scores and failure categorization matching what Langfuse/Phoenix/Opik would show."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Export a week of OTel traces to Langfuse cloud (free tier). Which sessions failed? Why?\n2. Write an LLM-judge rubric for your domain (factual correctness, tone, scope adherence). Test on 50 traces.\n3. Compare Langfuse prompt versioning against Phoenix's trace clustering. Which tells you what broke faster?\n4. Read Opik's guardrail docs. Wire a PII redaction guardrail to one of your agent runs.\n5. Benchmark the three on your corpus. Ignore vendor-published numbers; measure your own."
      ]
    }
